/-!
# The image of a hypercovering under a continuous functor

Let `C` and `D` be sites given by pretopologies `JC` and `JD`, both with fibre products, and let
`u : D ⥤ C` be a functor which takes covering families to covering families and preserves fibre
products. Applying `u` to every component of every semi-representable object in every simplicial
degree turns a hypercovering of `Y : D` into a hypercovering of `u Y`.

This is Tag 0DAZ. The degree-zero clause is
`Stacks.CategoryTheory.Hypercovering.IsHypercovering.map_zero`, proved in
`StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Hypercovering.Basic`; what is added here is the clause in
degree `n + 1`, which needs the comparison of the `n`-coskeleton of the image with the image of
the `n`-coskeleton, and hence the fact that the degreewise image functor preserves finite limits.

## Main definitions

* `CategoryTheory.Limits.isLimitPullbackConeMkOfEq`: transport of a limit pullback cone along an
  equality of one of the legs of the cospan.
* `Stacks.CategoryTheory.Hypercovering.pullbackConeMapFormalCoproduct` and
  `isLimitPullbackConeMapFormalCoproduct`: the componentwise fibre product cones of the image of a
  cospan of semi-representable objects, and their limit property.
* `Stacks.CategoryTheory.Hypercovering.isTerminalMapFormalCoproductTerminal`: the image of the
  terminal semi-representable object under a functor preserving terminal objects is terminal.
* `Stacks.CategoryTheory.Hypercovering.finCategoryStructuredArrowInclusionOp`: the shape
  `(Δ/⦋m⦌)_{≤n}` of the limit formula defining the `n`-coskeleton is a finite category.

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.Over.preservesFiniteLimitsPost`: a functor preserving fibre products induces a
  functor of slice categories which preserves finite limits. This is the argument of the source:
  the functor preserves the terminal object `𝟙 Y` of `D/Y` because that object goes to `𝟙 (u Y)`,
  and it preserves fibre products because the forgetful functor of a slice category creates
  connected limits.
* `Stacks.CategoryTheory.Hypercovering.preservesFiniteLimitsMapFormalCoproduct`: the degreewise
  image functor on semi-representable objects preserves finite limits as soon as the underlying
  functor does. Finite limits of formal coproducts are built from the terminal object and the
  fibre products, and both are computed componentwise with the index types unchanged.
* `Stacks.CategoryTheory.Hypercovering.preservesPointwiseRightKanExtensionAtInclusionOp`: a
  functor preserving finite limits preserves the pointwise right Kan extensions along
  `(Δ_{≤n} ⊆ Δ)ᵒᵖ` which define the `n`-coskeleton.
* `Stacks.CategoryTheory.Hypercovering.exists_iso_map_coskAdj_unit_app`: the coskeleton
  comparison. The image of the degree-`x` component of the unit of the `n`-coskeleton adjunction
  of `K` becomes, after one isomorphism, the degree-`x` component of the unit of the
  `n`-coskeleton adjunction of `K ⋙ F`.
* `Stacks.CategoryTheory.Hypercovering.IsHypercovering.map`: **Tag 0DAZ**.

## Implementation notes

The hypothesis on `u` is `MapsCoveringsToCoverings`, which is clause (1) of the definition of a
continuous functor in Tag 00WV: the image family `{u Vᵢ → u V}` of a covering family is a covering
family. Clause (2), preservation of fibre products, is the
`PreservesLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan u` instance. This is the hypothesis the source states, and
it is not interchangeable with the condition that the sieve generated by the image family be a
covering: coverings of a pretopology need not be downward closed, so the two conditions are
incomparable, and only the image-family form implies that covering morphisms of semi-representable
objects map to covering morphisms. See the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Hypercovering.Basic`.

The componentwise fibre products of formal coproducts are taken from
`StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.CoveringPermanence` rather than from Mathlib, for the reason
recorded there: the binder type of the family-of-cones argument of
`CategoryTheory.Limits.FormalCoproduct.pullbackCone` mentions `eqToHom (by rw [i.2])`, which the
elaborator lifts to a constant private to Mathlib's own module, so any reference to that
declaration or to its universal property fails in the kernel. For the same reason every binder
here writes the comparison as `eqToHom (congrArg _ i.2)`.

The finiteness of the shape `(Δ/⦋m⦌)_{≤n}` is reproved here. It is established in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicTopology.SimplicialObject.Coskeletal.Existence`, but the three declarations
that carry it there are `private`.

The coskeleton comparison is stated as the existence of an isomorphism in each degree rather than
as a named isomorphism of functors. The two functors `cosk_n(K) ⋙ F` and `cosk_n(K ⋙ F)` extend
the same truncated object, but their counits land in the two spellings `(L ⋙ K) ⋙ F` and
`L ⋙ (K ⋙ F)` of one functor, which agree definitionally and not syntactically; stating only the
existence keeps that bookkeeping inside the proof, where ascribed local abbreviations fix it.
The comparison of the two units is the argument of
`CategoryTheory.Functor.whiskerRight_eq_of_isRightKanExtension` in
`StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Hypercovering.Injectives`, carried out inline rather than by
importing that module, which lies above this one in the development.

The index universe `w` of the formal coproducts stays independent of the universes of `C` and `D`
throughout, as it is in Tags 01G3 and 01G5.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DAZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DAZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00WV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00WV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01G5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01G5)
-/

@[expose] public section

universe w v₁ v₂ u₁ u₂

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite Simplicial

namespace CategoryTheory.Limits

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C]

/-- A limit pullback cone stays a limit pullback cone when one leg of the cospan is replaced by
an equal morphism. -/
def isLimitPullbackConeMkOfEq {X Y Z : C} {a a' : X ⟶ Z} {b : Y ⟶ Z} (e : a = a')
    (c : PullbackCone a b) (hc : IsLimit c) :
    IsLimit (PullbackCone.mk c.fst c.snd
      (show c.fst ≫ a' = c.snd ≫ b by rw [← e]; exact c.condition) : PullbackCone a' b) := by
  subst e
  exact IsLimit.ofIsoLimit hc
    (PullbackCone.ext (Iso.refl _) (Category.id_comp _).symm (Category.id_comp _).symm)

end CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace CategoryTheory.Over

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] {D : Type u₂} [Category.{v₂} D] (u : D ⥤ C) (Y : D)

/-- A functor preserving connected limits of a given shape induces a functor of slice categories
preserving limits of that shape, because the forgetful functor of a slice category creates
connected limits. -/
theorem preservesLimitsOfShapePostOfIsConnected (J : Type*) [Category J] [IsConnected J]
    [PreservesLimitsOfShape J u] : PreservesLimitsOfShape J (Over.post u (X := Y)) where
  preservesLimit {K} := by
    have : PreservesLimit K (Over.post u (X := Y) ⋙ Over.forget (u.obj Y)) := by
      rw [Over.post_forget_eq_forget_comp]
      infer_instance
    exact preservesLimit_of_reflects_of_preserves _ (Over.forget (u.obj Y))

/-- The induced functor of slice categories preserves the terminal object: the terminal object of
`D/Y` is `𝟙 Y`, and it is sent to `u (𝟙 Y) = 𝟙 (u Y)`. -/
theorem preservesLimitsOfShapePEmptyPost :
    PreservesLimitsOfShape (Discrete.{0} PEmpty) (Over.post u (X := Y)) := by
  have hT : IsTerminal ((Over.post u (X := Y)).obj (⊤_ (Over Y))) := by
    have hid : IsTerminal (Over.mk (u.map (𝟙 Y))) := by
      rw [CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id]
      exact Over.mkIdTerminal
    exact hid.ofIso ((Over.post u (X := Y)).mapIso
      (terminalIsTerminal.uniqueUpToIso Over.mkIdTerminal)).symm
  have : PreservesLimit (Functor.empty.{0} (Over Y)) (Over.post u (X := Y)) :=
    preservesTerminal_of_iso _ (hT.uniqueUpToIso terminalIsTerminal)
  exact preservesLimitsOfShape_pempty_of_preservesTerminal _

/-- **The slice half of Tag 0DAZ's hypothesis.** A functor preserving fibre products induces a
functor of slice categories preserving all finite limits. -/
theorem preservesFiniteLimitsPost [HasPullbacks D] [PreservesLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan u] :
    PreservesFiniteLimits (Over.post u (X := Y)) := by
  have := preservesLimitsOfShapePEmptyPost u Y
  have := preservesLimitsOfShapePostOfIsConnected u Y WalkingCospan
  exact preservesFiniteLimits_of_preservesTerminal_and_pullbacks _

end CategoryTheory.Over

namespace Stacks.CategoryTheory.Hypercovering

open _root_.CategoryTheory _root_.CategoryTheory.Limits

section FormalCoproduct

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] {D : Type u₂} [Category.{v₂} D] (F : D ⥤ C)

section Pullback

variable [PreservesLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan F] {X Y Z : FormalCoproduct.{w} D}
  (f : X ⟶ Z) (g : Y ⟶ Z)

section Cones

variable (pb : ∀ i : Function.Pullback f.f g.f,
    PullbackCone (f.φ i.1.1 ≫ eqToHom (congrArg Z.obj i.2)) (g.φ i.1.2))
  (hpb : ∀ i, IsLimit (pb i))

/-- The componentwise pullback cones of the image of a cospan of semi-representable objects: the
index types of a pullback of formal coproducts are unchanged by a degreewise functor, so the
image cones are indexed by the very same type. -/
def pullbackConeMapFormalCoproduct (i : Function.Pullback f.f g.f) :
    PullbackCone (F.map (f.φ i.1.1) ≫ eqToHom (congrArg (fun k ↦ F.obj (Z.obj k)) i.2))
      (F.map (g.φ i.1.2)) :=
  PullbackCone.mk ((pb i).map F).fst ((pb i).map F).snd (by
    have h := congrArg F.map (pb i).condition
    simp only [F.map_comp, eqToHom_map] at h
    exact h)

/-- The componentwise image cones of `pullbackConeMapFormalCoproduct` are limits, because `F`
preserves the componentwise pullbacks. -/
noncomputable def isLimitPullbackConeMapFormalCoproduct (i : Function.Pullback f.f g.f) :
    IsLimit (pullbackConeMapFormalCoproduct F f g pb i) := by
  refine isLimitPullbackConeMkOfEq
    (a := F.map (f.φ i.1.1 ≫ eqToHom (congrArg Z.obj i.2))) ?_ ((pb i).map F)
    ((PullbackCone.isLimitMapConeEquiv (pb i) F).1 (isLimitOfPreserves F (hpb i)))
  rw [F.map_comp, eqToHom_map]

end Cones

/-- The degreewise image functor preserves the pullback of a given cospan of semi-representable
objects: the index type of the pullback is unchanged, and the component at each index is the
image of a pullback in `D`. -/
theorem preservesLimitCospanMapFormalCoproduct [HasPullbacks D] :
    PreservesLimit (cospan f g) (mapFormalCoproduct.{w} F) := by
  let pb : ∀ i : Function.Pullback f.f g.f,
      PullbackCone (f.φ i.1.1 ≫ eqToHom (congrArg Z.obj i.2)) (g.φ i.1.2) :=
    pullbackConeFamily f g
  have hpb : ∀ i, IsLimit (pb i) := fun _ ↦ pullback.isLimit _ _
  let c := pullbackFormalCoproduct.cone f g pb
  refine preservesLimit_of_preserves_limit_cone
    (pullbackFormalCoproduct.isLimit f g pb hpb) ?_
  refine (PullbackCone.isLimitMapConeEquiv c (mapFormalCoproduct.{w} F)).2 ?_
  refine IsLimit.ofIsoLimit (pullbackFormalCoproduct.isLimit
    ((mapFormalCoproduct.{w} F).map f) ((mapFormalCoproduct.{w} F).map g)
    (pullbackConeMapFormalCoproduct F f g pb)
    (isLimitPullbackConeMapFormalCoproduct F f g pb hpb)) ?_
  exact PullbackCone.ext (Iso.refl _) (Category.id_comp _).symm (Category.id_comp _).symm

end Pullback

section Terminal

variable [HasTerminal C] [HasTerminal D] [PreservesLimitsOfShape (Discrete.{0} PEmpty) F]

/-- The image of the terminal semi-representable object under a functor preserving terminal
objects is terminal. -/
noncomputable def isTerminalMapFormalCoproductTerminal :
    IsTerminal ((mapFormalCoproduct.{w} F).obj (⊤_ (FormalCoproduct.{w} D))) :=
  (FormalCoproduct.isTerminalIncl (F.obj (⊤_ D)) (terminalIsTerminal.isTerminalObj F)).ofIso
    ((mapFormalCoproduct.{w} F).mapIso (terminalIsTerminal.uniqueUpToIso
      (FormalCoproduct.isTerminalIncl (⊤_ D) terminalIsTerminal))).symm

/-- The degreewise image functor preserves the terminal object. -/
theorem preservesLimitsOfShapePEmptyMapFormalCoproduct :
    PreservesLimitsOfShape (Discrete.{0} PEmpty) (mapFormalCoproduct.{w} F) := by
  have : PreservesLimit (Functor.empty.{0} (FormalCoproduct.{w} D)) (mapFormalCoproduct.{w} F) :=
    preservesTerminal_of_iso _
      ((isTerminalMapFormalCoproductTerminal.{w} F).uniqueUpToIso terminalIsTerminal)
  exact preservesLimitsOfShape_pempty_of_preservesTerminal _

end Terminal

section FiniteLimits

variable [HasPullbacks D] [PreservesFiniteLimits F]

/-- The degreewise image functor preserves all pullbacks. -/
theorem preservesLimitsOfShapeWalkingCospanMapFormalCoproduct :
    PreservesLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan (mapFormalCoproduct.{w} F) where
  preservesLimit {K} := by
    have : PreservesLimit (cospan (K.map WalkingCospan.Hom.inl) (K.map WalkingCospan.Hom.inr))
        (mapFormalCoproduct.{w} F) :=
      preservesLimitCospanMapFormalCoproduct F _ _
    exact preservesLimit_of_iso_diagram _ (diagramIsoCospan K).symm

/-- **The semi-representable half of Tag 0DAZ's hypothesis.** The degreewise image functor on
semi-representable objects preserves finite limits as soon as the underlying functor does: finite
limits of formal coproducts come from the terminal object and the pullbacks, and both are computed
componentwise with the index types unchanged. -/
theorem preservesFiniteLimitsMapFormalCoproduct [HasTerminal C] [HasTerminal D] :
    PreservesFiniteLimits (mapFormalCoproduct.{w} F) := by
  have := preservesLimitsOfShapePEmptyMapFormalCoproduct.{w} F
  have := preservesLimitsOfShapeWalkingCospanMapFormalCoproduct.{w} F
  exact preservesFiniteLimits_of_preservesTerminal_and_pullbacks _

end FiniteLimits

end FormalCoproduct

section Coskeleton

open SimplicialObject

/-- The shape `(Δ/⦋m⦌)_{≤n} = StructuredArrow Y (Δ_{≤n} ⊆ Δ)ᵒᵖ` has finitely many objects: an
object is a `n`-truncated simplex together with a morphism to it. -/
theorem finiteStructuredArrowInclusionOp (n : ℕ) (m : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ) :
    Finite (StructuredArrow m (SimplexCategory.Truncated.inclusion n).op) := by
  have := SimplicialObject.Truncated.finite_truncated n
  have : Finite (SimplexCategory.Truncated n)ᵒᵖ := .of_equiv _ equivToOpposite
  have : ∀ A : (SimplexCategory.Truncated n)ᵒᵖ,
      Finite (m ⟶ (SimplexCategory.Truncated.inclusion n).op.obj A) := fun _ ↦
    SimplicialObject.Truncated.finite_hom_op _ _
  refine Finite.of_injective (fun a ↦ (⟨a.right, a.hom⟩ :
    (A : (SimplexCategory.Truncated n)ᵒᵖ) ×
      (m ⟶ (SimplexCategory.Truncated.inclusion n).op.obj A))) ?_
  rintro ⟨l₁, r₁, w₁⟩ ⟨l₂, r₂, w₂⟩ h
  obtain ⟨rfl, h'⟩ := Sigma.mk.inj_iff.mp h
  obtain rfl := eq_of_heq h'
  cases l₁
  cases l₂
  rfl

/-- The hom types of the shape `(Δ/⦋m⦌)_{≤n}` are finite: a morphism there is determined by a
morphism of truncated simplices. -/
theorem finiteHomStructuredArrowInclusionOp (n : ℕ) (m : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ)
    (A A' : StructuredArrow m (SimplexCategory.Truncated.inclusion n).op) : Finite (A ⟶ A') := by
  have : Finite (A.right ⟶ A'.right) :=
    have := SimplicialObject.Truncated.finite_hom_fullSubcategory A'.right.unop A.right.unop
    SimplicialObject.Truncated.finite_hom_op A.right A'.right
  exact .of_injective CommaMorphism.right fun _ _ h ↦ StructuredArrow.hom_ext _ _ h

/-- The shape of the limit formula defining the `n`-coskeleton is a finite category. -/
@[instance_reducible]
noncomputable def finCategoryStructuredArrowInclusionOp (n : ℕ) (m : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ) :
    FinCategory (StructuredArrow m (SimplexCategory.Truncated.inclusion n).op) where
  fintypeObj := @Fintype.ofFinite _ (finiteStructuredArrowInclusionOp n m)
  fintypeHom A A' := @Fintype.ofFinite _ (finiteHomStructuredArrowInclusionOp n m A A')

variable {B : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} B] {E : Type u₂} [Category.{v₂} E]
/-- The comparison of the coskeleton units for a functor preserving the pointwise right Kan
extensions along `(Δ_{≤n} ⊆ Δ)ᵒᵖ`. -/
private theorem exists_iso_map_coskAdj_unit_app_of_preserves (n : ℕ) (K : SimplicialObject B)
    (F : B ⥤ E) [F.PreservesPointwiseRightKanExtensions (SimplexCategory.Truncated.inclusion n).op]
    [∀ Z : SimplicialObject.Truncated B n,
      (SimplexCategory.Truncated.inclusion n).op.HasPointwiseRightKanExtension Z]
    [∀ Z : SimplicialObject.Truncated E n,
      (SimplexCategory.Truncated.inclusion n).op.HasPointwiseRightKanExtension Z]
    (x : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ) :
    ∃ e : ((cosk n).obj K ⋙ F).obj x ≅ ((cosk n).obj (K ⋙ F)).obj x,
      F.map (((coskAdj n).unit.app K).app x) ≫ e.hom =
        ((coskAdj n).unit.app (K ⋙ F)).app x := by
  let L : (SimplexCategory.Truncated n)ᵒᵖ ⥤ SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ :=
    (SimplexCategory.Truncated.inclusion n).op
  let X : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ ⥤ B := K
  let XF : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ ⥤ E := X ⋙ F
  let Y : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ ⥤ B := (Truncated.cosk n).obj ((truncation n).obj X)
  let α : L ⋙ Y ⟶ L ⋙ X := (coskAdj n).counit.app ((truncation n).obj X)
  let η₀ : X ⟶ Y := (coskAdj n).unit.app X
  let Z : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ ⥤ E := (Truncated.cosk n).obj ((truncation n).obj XF)
  let ε : L ⋙ Z ⟶ L ⋙ X ⋙ F := (coskAdj n).counit.app ((truncation n).obj XF)
  let η : X ⋙ F ⟶ Z := (coskAdj n).unit.app XF
  let εs := (Functor.associator _ _ _).inv ≫ Functor.whiskerRight α F
  let _ : F.PreservesPointwiseRightKanExtension (L ⋙ X) L := fun _ ↦ inferInstance
  let _ : F.PreservesRightKanExtension (L ⋙ X) L := inferInstance
  let _ : Y.IsRightKanExtension α := by
    change ((cosk n).obj X).IsRightKanExtension ((coskAdj n).counit.app ((truncation n).obj X))
    infer_instance
  let _ : Z.IsRightKanExtension ε := by
    change ((cosk n).obj XF).IsRightKanExtension ((coskAdj n).counit.app ((truncation n).obj XF))
    infer_instance
  let e := Functor.rightKanExtensionUnique (Y ⋙ F) εs Z ε
  have he : L.whiskerLeft e.hom ≫ ε = εs := by
    simp [e, Functor.rightKanExtensionUnique, Functor.liftOfIsRightKanExtension_fac, εs]
  have hη₀ : L.whiskerLeft η₀ ≫ α = 𝟙 (L ⋙ X) := (coskAdj n).left_triangle_components X
  have hη : L.whiskerLeft η ≫ ε = 𝟙 (L ⋙ X ⋙ F) := (coskAdj n).left_triangle_components XF
  have hunit : Functor.whiskerRight η₀ F ≫ e.hom = η := by
    refine Functor.hom_ext_of_isRightKanExtension Z ε _ _ ?_
    ext a
    have heapp : e.hom.app (L.obj a) ≫ ε.app a =
        ((Functor.associator _ _ _).inv ≫ Functor.whiskerRight α F).app a := by
      simpa only [εs, NatTrans.comp_app, Functor.whiskerLeft_app] using
        NatTrans.congr_app he a
    have h₀ := NatTrans.congr_app hη₀ a
    have h₁ := NatTrans.congr_app hη a
    simp only [Functor.whiskerLeft_app, NatTrans.comp_app] at h₀ h₁
    simp only [Functor.whiskerLeft_app, NatTrans.comp_app]
    rw [Category.assoc, heapp]
    simp only [Functor.associator_inv_app, Functor.whiskerRight_app, NatTrans.comp_app,
      Category.id_comp]
    rw [← F.map_comp, h₀]
    simpa using h₁.symm
  exact ⟨e.app x, by simpa [η₀, η, X] using NatTrans.congr_app hunit x⟩


/-- A functor preserving finite limits preserves the pointwise right Kan extensions along
`(Δ_{≤n} ⊆ Δ)ᵒᵖ` which define the `n`-coskeleton, because the shape of the limit formula is a
finite category. -/
instance preservesPointwiseRightKanExtensionAtInclusionOp (F : B ⥤ E) [PreservesFiniteLimits F]
    (n : ℕ) (Z : SimplicialObject.Truncated B n) (m : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ) :
    F.PreservesPointwiseRightKanExtensionAt Z (SimplexCategory.Truncated.inclusion n).op m := by
  have := finCategoryStructuredArrowInclusionOp n m
  infer_instance

variable (n : ℕ) (K : SimplicialObject B) (F : B ⥤ E) [PreservesFiniteLimits F]
  [∀ Z : SimplicialObject.Truncated B n,
    (SimplexCategory.Truncated.inclusion n).op.HasPointwiseRightKanExtension Z]
  [∀ Z : SimplicialObject.Truncated E n,
    (SimplexCategory.Truncated.inclusion n).op.HasPointwiseRightKanExtension Z]

/-- Every `n`-truncated simplicial object of `B` has a right Kan extension along
`(Δ_{≤n} ⊆ Δ)ᵒᵖ`. -/
instance hasRightKanExtensionInclusionOpSource : ∀ Z : SimplicialObject.Truncated B n,
    (SimplexCategory.Truncated.inclusion n).op.HasRightKanExtension Z := fun Z ↦
  ((SimplexCategory.Truncated.inclusion n).op.isPointwiseRightKanExtensionRanCounit
    Z).hasRightKanExtension

/-- Every `n`-truncated simplicial object of `E` has a right Kan extension along
`(Δ_{≤n} ⊆ Δ)ᵒᵖ`. -/
instance hasRightKanExtensionInclusionOpTarget : ∀ Z : SimplicialObject.Truncated E n,
    (SimplexCategory.Truncated.inclusion n).op.HasRightKanExtension Z := fun Z ↦
  ((SimplexCategory.Truncated.inclusion n).op.isPointwiseRightKanExtensionRanCounit
    Z).hasRightKanExtension

/-- **The coskeleton comparison of Tag 0DAZ.** Let `F` preserve finite limits. Then in each
simplicial degree the image under `F` of the degree-`x` component of the unit of the
`n`-coskeleton adjunction of `K` becomes, after one isomorphism, the degree-`x` component of the
unit of the `n`-coskeleton adjunction of `K ⋙ F`.

Both `cosk_n(K) ⋙ F` and `cosk_n(K ⋙ F)` are right Kan extensions of the `n`-truncation of
`K ⋙ F` along `(Δ_{≤n} ⊆ Δ)ᵒᵖ` — the first because `F` preserves the pointwise right Kan
extensions defining the coskeleton — so they agree up to a unique isomorphism compatible with the
counits, and that isomorphism also matches the units. -/
theorem exists_iso_map_coskAdj_unit_app (x : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ) :
    ∃ e : ((cosk n).obj K ⋙ F).obj x ≅ ((cosk n).obj (K ⋙ F)).obj x,
      F.map (((coskAdj n).unit.app K).app x) ≫ e.hom =
        ((coskAdj n).unit.app (K ⋙ F)).app x := by
  have : F.PreservesPointwiseRightKanExtensions (SimplexCategory.Truncated.inclusion n).op :=
    fun _ _ ↦ inferInstance
  exact exists_iso_map_coskAdj_unit_app_of_preserves n K F x

end Coskeleton

section CoskeletonOfKanExtensions

open SimplicialObject

variable {B : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} B] {E : Type u₂} [Category.{v₂} E]

/-! The comparison of Tag 0DAZ for a functor that only preserves the pointwise right Kan
extensions defining the coskeleton (for instance `T ⨯ -`, which preserves connected limits). -/

variable (n : ℕ) (K : SimplicialObject B) (F : B ⥤ E)
  [F.PreservesPointwiseRightKanExtensions (SimplexCategory.Truncated.inclusion n).op]
  [∀ Z : SimplicialObject.Truncated B n,
    (SimplexCategory.Truncated.inclusion n).op.HasPointwiseRightKanExtension Z]
  [∀ Z : SimplicialObject.Truncated E n,
    (SimplexCategory.Truncated.inclusion n).op.HasPointwiseRightKanExtension Z]

/-- **The coskeleton comparison of Tag 0DAZ.** Let `F` preserve the pointwise right Kan
extensions along `(Δ_{≤n} ⊆ Δ)ᵒᵖ` which define the `n`-coskeleton — by
`preservesPointwiseRightKanExtensionAtInclusionOp` it is enough that `F` preserve finite limits.
Then in each simplicial degree the image under `F` of the degree-`x` component of the unit of the
`n`-coskeleton adjunction of `K` becomes, after one isomorphism, the degree-`x` component of the
unit of the `n`-coskeleton adjunction of `K ⋙ F`.

Both `cosk_n(K) ⋙ F` and `cosk_n(K ⋙ F)` are right Kan extensions of the `n`-truncation of
`K ⋙ F` along `(Δ_{≤n} ⊆ Δ)ᵒᵖ` — the first because `F` preserves the pointwise right Kan
extensions defining the coskeleton — so they agree up to a unique isomorphism compatible with the
counits, and that isomorphism also matches the units.

The hypothesis is the preservation of those Kan extensions rather than of finite limits because
the shapes `(Δ/⦋m⦌)_{≤n}` are not merely finite but, for `n ≥ 1`, connected: a functor such as
`T ⨯ -` which preserves only connected limits still preserves these coskeleta, which is what
Stacks 01GE base-changed along a presheaf of sets needs. -/
theorem exists_iso_map_coskAdj_unit_app' (x : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ) :
    ∃ e : ((cosk n).obj K ⋙ F).obj x ≅ ((cosk n).obj (K ⋙ F)).obj x,
      F.map (((coskAdj n).unit.app K).app x) ≫ e.hom =
        ((coskAdj n).unit.app (K ⋙ F)).app x := by
  exact exists_iso_map_coskAdj_unit_app_of_preserves n K F x

end CoskeletonOfKanExtensions

section Map

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] [HasPullbacks C]
  {D : Type u₂} [Category.{v₂} D] [HasPullbacks D]

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0DAZ.** Let `u : D ⥤ C` be a functor between sites given by
pretopologies which takes covering families to covering families and preserves fibre products.
Then the degreewise image under `u` of a hypercovering of `Y : D` is a hypercovering of `u Y`. -/
@[stacks 0DAZ "the hypothesis that `u` be continuous is used only through its covering clause \
  `MapsCoveringsToCoverings`, which is Tag 00WV(1) verbatim — the same index type and the same \
  image family — together with the preservation of fibre products that is Tag 00WV(2); the \
  conclusion is the full statement, both the degree-zero clause and the clause in degree n + 1"]
theorem IsHypercovering.map (JD : Pretopology D) (JC : Pretopology C) (u : D ⥤ C)
    (hu : MapsCoveringsToCoverings.{w} u JD JC) [PreservesLimitsOfShape WalkingCospan u] {Y : D}
    (K : SimplicialObject (FormalCoproduct.{w} (Over Y)))
    (hK : IsHypercovering JD K) :
    IsHypercovering JC (K ⋙ mapFormalCoproduct.{w} (Over.post u)) := by
  have hpost : PreservesFiniteLimits (Over.post u (X := Y)) := Over.preservesFiniteLimitsPost u Y
  have hmap : PreservesFiniteLimits (mapFormalCoproduct.{w} (Over.post u (X := Y))) :=
    preservesFiniteLimitsMapFormalCoproduct.{w} _
  refine ⟨IsHypercovering.map_zero u Y hu hK.1, fun n ↦ ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := exists_iso_map_coskAdj_unit_app n K
    (mapFormalCoproduct.{w} (Over.post u (X := Y))) (op ⦋n + 1⦌)
  rw [← he]
  exact ((hK.2 n).map hu).comp_isIso JC e.hom

end Map

end Stacks.CategoryTheory.Hypercovering

